ants  there was a lady who started a gym they  wanted to expand there was a contractor  who wanted to expand who  had a government contract but they  needed the capital to finance it if you  want to visit the government you have to  show  that you have the wherewithal and so we  went in and we got them the help they  needed it might be a lawyer it might be  an accountant  but it certainly was a loan and helped  them expand and it's a wonderful thing  and a lot of those business members they  hire locally  so it helps the community twice yeah  they expand as a business and they hire  locally  jamie it's anthony uh i i wanted to ask  you about the the banking business which  which is not known for its diversity  what are you doing at jp morgan chase to  ensure diversity in the company  yeah so we we've been working on  diversity for a long time in fact  we've doubled down that too so like  black eds and md's in this company are  up 50  in the last three years hiring training  recruiting  half of my direct reports are women and  we just had a woman who was a fabulous  woman was running our  whole retail system as part of my  management committee who just left to  run another company but we're doing  everything we can to this company to  help  the black community you were part of a  group of business leaders that met with  president biden vice president harris  and treasury secretary yellen uh  recently  did you talk about the the democrats 1.9  trillion dollar  stimulus bill and how do you feel about  it do you think it's  enough do you think it's too much  yeah so we did so first of all i was  grateful the president and the vice  president had us in  there were four ceos in the room we  spent almost two hours  and we actually covered a lot of ground  from the from that bill to  immigration to taxation to and i love  the fact he brought  american competitiveness we need to make  sure america is competitive for the next  hundred years and  not just to get through covet 